  "feature_reconstruction_notes": {
    "amplitude": "Use the 0–500 ms matched cohort and fixed training amplitude scaling from ablation.json. Pool over ten 50 ms bins (amp_bin50, PCA, GRF, continuous encoders) or over the whole window (amp_mean); flatten bin-major for the readouts apart from the temporal encoders.",
    "voltage": "At each channel standardize on unique matched training samples, then mean-pool over ten 50 ms bins.",
    "wavelet_covariance": "At zero-based frequency indices 2, 6, and 9 use unscaled exp(log amplitude) times cosine phase. Fit Ledoit–Wolf per trial and band over time, flooring eigenvalues at 1e-6 times the maximum eigenvalue. Log-Euclidean: vectorize diagonal and sqrt(2)-weighted upper triangle. Tangent: use a separate training-fitted Riemannian reference per band, then concatenate.",
    "grf": "For each trial and electrode solve (1.01 I + lambda L) x = standardized binned amplitude, with L the four-neighbor 10-by-12 time-frequency grid Laplacian.",
    "minirocket": "Use the unpooled standardized amplitude in trial-by-feature-by-time order.",
    "cebra": "Archived 500 ms wavelet encoder uses the 1000-update CEBRA recipe in ablation.json; average over valid receptive-field centers.",
